  "workspaceComments": [
   {
    "text": "Output: the trained driver senses the world (speed, tilt, ground radar …), runs those numbers through its network to score each action, does the action, and repeats until the try is over. Then it's your turn with the arrow keys!",
    "width": 380,
    "height": 130,
    "x": 980,
    "y": 659
   },
   {
    "text": "Things to try: make the terrain 'steps' or 'mixed', add 'can jump' or 'can rocket boost', remove a sense and see if it still learns, change the rewards (reward speed? punish energy?), or switch 'same world every try' off so it must handle any terrain.",
    "width": 380,
    "height": 130,
    "x": 980,
    "y": 819
   }
  ]
